KONOHAGAKURE — HOKAGE SUCCESSION PROTOCOL

The Hokage is the leader and strongest protector of the Hidden Leaf. Succession preserves stability and the Will of Fire.

Protocol:
- A successor is customarily nominated by the sitting or outgoing Hokage, or recommended by the Village Council and elders.
- The appointment is confirmed by the Fire Daimyo and recognized by the shinobi of the village.
- In the event of the Hokage's death or incapacity, the Council may appoint an interim leader until a successor is installed.
- The chosen Hokage must embody the Will of Fire and command the trust of the village.

Lineage of the office: Hashirama Senju (First) → Tobirama Senju (Second) → Hiruzen Sarutobi (Third) → Minato Namikaze (Fourth) → Tsunade Senju (Fifth), and onward. Full succession records are held separately in the Hokage Office archive.
Issued by the Office of the Hokage.
